  "testIds": [
    "a settings deny blocks with [Permission] and the hook never runs",
    "a version bump re-requires trust",
    "audits every non-applicable product boundary without claiming parity",
    "bare `*` deny matches every tool",
    "binds mid-turn approval to operation fingerprint and record revision",
    "collectHooks fires non-tool Notification hooks (matcher null/*)",
    "detects a quoted PowerShell destination outside the workspace",
    "detects untracked work when status.showUntrackedFiles is disabled",
    "does not let CC_SANDBOX_DISABLE bypass strict mode",
    "drops credential files (returns null)",
    "fails closed on a PowerShell variable write target",
    "falls back to terminal confirm when the IDE dies mid-review",
    "isolates permission authority at the nearest nested repository",
    "keeps device-namespace rejection while Cygwin symlink parity remains reverted",
    "keeps input redirection behind the shell approval gate",
    "keeps the complete source and destination visible in the grant",
    "keeps zsh conditional commands behind destructive safety classification",
    "lets configuration disable Remote Control but never widen it",
    "makes tabs and invisible Unicode explicit without changing the executed arguments",
    "redacts JWT and AWS credentials while preserving the complete approval target",
    "refuses filesystem, drive, UNC-share, and user-home roots",
    "rejects bypassPermissions when managed policy disables it",
    "rejects pre-positioned POSIX socket paths and authenticates Windows named pipes",
    "rejects raw Git blob or object approval input before contacting the IDE",
    "requires live confirmation for destructive Git in the primary checkout despite a settings allow",
    "runs with a clean environment and never inherits credential variables",
    "suppresses stderr content and coalesces bounded diagnostics",
    "treats a trailing slash deny target as the same canonical path",
    "uses the rule name for settings/hook ask rules"
